auth:
  symbol: "#auth-route"
  description: >
    Public account endpoints backing the storefront. POST /auth/signup creates a
    user (409 email_taken on conflict), POST /auth/login verifies credentials; both
    return { token, user } where token is a signed JWT from #auth-service. Login
    returns a generic 401 invalid_credentials without revealing which field failed.
    No gate — these are the entry points that mint the ^authenticated token.
  signals: [!user-registered, !user-logged-in]

products:
  symbol: "#products-route"
  description: >
    Public catalog read (GET /products) for the storefront. No auth — browsing is
    anonymous; ^authenticated only applies at /checkout. Prices returned as strings
    (Postgres numeric) so the client never does float math on money.

checkout:
  symbol: "#checkout-route"
  description: >
    The HUMAN (in-browser) leg of $checkout-flow. POST /checkout requires a user-audience
    JWT (^authenticated); an agent grant is rejected here so it can't bypass the selfie
    path. Recomputes price server-side, enforces ^checkout-authorized (per-tx/daily caps
    via #orders-service, plus a 428 confirmation_required above the $10 auto-approve
    threshold), then charges immediately via #payment-service. Shares all order/spend
    primitives with #agent-route through #orders-service. Full design in
    .paradigm/specs/wallet-checkout.md.
  gates: [^authenticated, ^checkout-authorized]
  signals: [!payment-submitted]

agent:
  symbol: "#agent-route"
  description: >
    The agentic-commerce entry points, called by a merchant MCP holding an agent grant.
    POST /agent/grant (^authenticated) mints the ^agent-authorized grant for a signed-in
    human. POST /agent/checkout (^agent-authorized + ^checkout-authorized) validates and
    reprices, applies spend caps, then creates a PENDING order + a verification session
    and returns 202 verification_required with a human-facing selfie URL — it NEVER
    charges. GET /agent/purchase/:orderId (^agent-authorized) polls the outcome, scoped
    to the grant's own user. Implements $agent-purchase-flow; reuses #orders-service and
    #payment-service so both checkout legs stay in lockstep.
  gates: [^agent-authorized, ^checkout-authorized]
  signals: [!agent-grant-issued, !agent-purchase-initiated]

verify:
  symbol: "#verify-route"
  description: >
    Human-facing ^personhood-verified checkpoint for agent-initiated purchases, opened
    from a link the agent surfaced. Two modes (#worldid-service): in MOCK, GET
    /verify/:sessionId renders a click-through page that settles the order (disabled in
    world mode so it can't bypass the selfie). In WORLD, the SPA renders the World ID
    Selfie Check widget, reads GET /verify-context/:sessionId for the RP signature, and
    POSTs the proof to POST /verify/:sessionId, which verifies it with World before
    settling. Settlement is shared and single-use (via #verification-service +
    #payment-service) either way.
  gates: [^personhood-verified]
  signals: [!personhood-verified, !purchase-completed]

circle-webhook:
  symbol: "#circle-webhook-route"
  description: >
    Receives Circle transaction-state webhooks. Source of truth for terminal
    payment state (COMPLETE/FAILED/DENIED/CANCELLED); updates orders idempotently
    by Circle transaction id. Full design in .paradigm/specs/wallet-checkout.md.
  gates: [^webhook-signature-verified]
  signals: [!payment-confirmed, !payment-failed]
  implementation_plan:
    webhook_signature_verified: >
      Verify X-Circle-Signature (base64 ECDSA over the RAW body) against the public key
      for X-Circle-Key-Id (GET Circle's /v2/notifications/publicKey/{keyId}, cache
      in-process). 401 on missing headers, unknown key id, or bad signature. Requires raw
      body bytes — server/src/index.ts's global express.json() currently discards these;
      switch to express.json({ verify: (req,_res,buf) => { req.rawBody = buf } }) (or a
      route-scoped express.raw()) so this route can verify before parsing.
    order_update: >
      Map Circle's transactionId + state to an `orders` row via
      `update orders set status = $1, updated_at = now() where circle_transaction_id = $2`
      (COMPLETE -> confirmed, FAILED/DENIED/CANCELLED -> matching lowercase status).
      Idempotent by construction — replays set the same terminal value. Emit
      !payment-confirmed / !payment-failed after the row update.
